    "turn_text": "Hi everyone, I'm Katie Couric and this is Next Question. It's hard to believe, but the 2024 election is less than a year away. What's even harder to believe, as Yogi Berra would say, it's deja vu all over again. Yep, that's right. Biden versus Trump. We've been hearing a lot about the Republican side of the campaign with the Iowa caucuses and the New Hampshire primary, and now Super Tuesday is just over a month away. But we haven't been hearing as much from the current administration. That's why I was thrilled to jump on a train, brave the elements, and head to the Eisenhower executive office building to sit down with Vice President Kamala Harris. By the way, these interviews can be very stressful. She's an incredibly busy person, so they only gave me 30 minutes, and I had a lot to cover. Abortion, immigration, Israel, Gaza, the administration's historically low approval ratings, despite their many accomplishments. Trump voters and some crucial voting blocks that don't necessarily think the second time's a charm. First of all, thank you so much for being",
