    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83368.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 94,
    "turn_text": "OK. I want to turn to the accomplishments of the Biden administration. Good. An infrastructure bill, finally, the CHIPS Act, the Safer Communities Act, addressing gun violence to name three legislative accomplishments. Low unemployment, millions of jobs created, inflation down, the stock market up. You don't hear that much from reporters do you in the form of a question? And yet, you and President Biden's approval ratings are at historic lows. The President at 38, you at 37, why do you think that is given what I just outlined?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_07",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "We are still in a crisis mode.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The public evaluates political performance primarily through the lens of ongoing crises rather than concrete achievements.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Historic low approval ratings reflect a perception of failure despite measurable policy successes.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Crisis mode shapes public judgment more strongly than economic indicators like job creation or inflation reduction.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "Reporters' narratives influence public perception more than tangible outcomes.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes that current conditions—despite progress—are still defined by instability or threat.",
        "confidence": 0.83
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Topic Shift"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 83368,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83368.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 95,
    "turn_text": "Well, first of all, if I listened to polls, I would have never run for my first office or probably my second or third for that matter. So we put so much stock in polls.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_06",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
